course: dictionary
lesson: 5612
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one to use. The word light is a good example. «Hold a magnifying glass over an ant and the bent light makes the ant look huge.» Here light means the rays that let us see, not something that weighs little.
explain: «On a summer evening a field can twinkle with fireflies, which are beetles making cold light in their tails.» Here light means the glow itself. Ask what would fit: a glow fits the sentence, but a weight does not. Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: Light can also mean not heavy, or pale in colour. «Light blue» is a pale shade, not a dark one. When you meet light, read the words around it, because the clues show which meaning you need.
fact: Light is what lets us see; it comes from the Sun, lamps and fire.
fact: A light is a lamp or bulb, as in «turn on the light».
fact: Light means not heavy, weighing little, as in «light as a feather».
fact: Light can also mean pale in colour, as in light blue, or gentle and small, as in a light rain.
fact: To light means to start a fire or make something burn or shine; its past form can be lit or lighted.
exercise: «Hold a magnifying glass over an ant and the bent light makes the ant look huge.» In this sentence, what is light? | A pale colour | A match to start a fire | Something that weighs very little | *The rays that let us see
exercise: «Please turn on the light, it is getting dark.» What does light mean here? | A gentle drizzle | *A lamp or bulb | A pale colour | Not heavy
exercise: «On a summer evening a field can twinkle with fireflies, which are beetles making cold light in their tails.» What does light mean here? | A heavy load | *A glow that you can see | Pale yellow paint | To start a fire
test: «Plants need light to grow, so keep the seedlings near a window.» What does light mean here? | To set fire to | *Sunshine and daylight that lets us see and helps plants grow | A pale colour | Not heavy
test: Ella says light blue is a shade of dark blue. What does light mean in «light blue»? | *Pale, not dark, in colour | Gentle and small | Dark | Heavy
exam: «Slow blinks mean a cat feels safe with you, while wide, round pupils in good light can mean it is scared or excited.» What does light mean in «good light»? | To start a fire | Pale colour | Heavy | *Bright daylight or lamp light that lets us see
